{
  "version": 3,
  "about": [
    "The production tree: every product, the workshop and station that make it, the education it needs, and its inputs. The game loads this file (embedded into Colony.Core): items, workshops, stations and recipes all come from here.",
    "Workshops are few and broad (DF-style): each is a room type whose recipes span several tiers. A recipe runs on one of the workshop's stations (machine parts, each built in sizes 1-5), so a workshop grows with the colony by adding stations rather than new rooms. Each placed machine is set to one of its station's recipes.",
    "To add a product: add an item and a recipe naming an existing workshop and station. Add a station only for a genuinely new process; add a workshop only for a new trade.",
    "Education gates recipes, not rooms: a worker may run a recipe at or below their level, so one Smelter has unskilled hands at the bloomery beside Scholars at the aether furnace.",
    "Tiers are not stored: a product's tier is 1 + the highest tier among its inputs (raw = 0).",
    "Counts are optional and rough for now: 'logs*2' in inputs, 'count' for outputs (default 1), 'ticks' for one run of labour (default 120 + 45 per tier: Balance.RecipeTicks).",
    "Home fixtures: 'material' is what a piece is mostly made of (wood, stone, metal, glass, cloth, clay: colonists may like one); 'place' says where a light or decor piece goes in a home (table, wall, floor, corner); 'fixture' names the home slot an item fills (bed, furniture, tableware, lighting, decor), 'tier' its quality (1 humble, 2 comfortable, 3 fine; each slot runs 1..n) and 'wear' the days it lasts in a home before it is replaced. Homes will be furnished by tier per slot, so upgrading means raising a tier, not refurnishing.",
    "'uses' entries of the form 'need: X' make an item satisfy colonists' need X (food; dress, household goods, comfort, health: the living standard). Foods give 'food' meals of nutrition per unit (a colonist eats about 3 a day).",
    "Station 'build' lists the material a machine is built from by size: one entry for all sizes; two for size 1 / sizes 2-5; three for size 1 / sizes 2-3 / sizes 4-5. Size 1 must be buildable before the station exists. 'model' picks the station's 3D stand-in (defaults to the station id).",
    "Item 'model' picks the pile shape the game draws; 'color' is its sRGB tint; 'stack' and 'carry' override the default stack and carry sizes.",
    "Education is acyclic: each level is taught from goods made by recipes of lower levels only. Teaching a level needs a teacher of that level, so founders bring a few Literates and a Scholar; the first Magister arrives as an event once the Academy has an attunement circle. Education recipes promote a colonist instead of making an item; 'worker' items (automatons) join the colony as workers.",
    "'uses' lists end uses outside the factory chain (needs, culture, construction, military, parts). Each workshop's 'later' lists products that would naturally slot in."
  ],
  "educationLevels": ["Unskilled", "Literate", "Scholar", "Magister"],
